{
  "why": "Mercury, by ear. Key pins (audio time, lane 0-3 = D F J K): 0:23.3-0:24.7, the violins' run up to the flutes starts S D F (lane 4 = the S ghost key) and then keeps the wave the user approved, J K D F J F J K D F J K, now that the bassoons' 47 comes before it instead of the 54 (user, Nov 24: 'I thought the run should start SDF and it seems to just go FJ'); 2:45.8, m.189: the first violins' climb 59 61 62 64 66 67 69 71 74 starts on D after the flute's J69 (not K59, a wrong-way drop) and waves up to K in its triplets, D F J | F J K | F J K, then the step down to 73 on J (the user likes D F J F J K waves; runs end on K going up; no ghost key here, user, Nov 24: 'I also don't like the ghost note in this section because this isn't really a run'); 2:48.7, m.192: after the borrowed step down, 85 79 74 81 85 83 goes K F D J K J (the engine had F79 D74 F81, the 79 and 81 on one key); 3:18.4-3:21.7, m.226-230: the second violins' line after the climb goes by triplet groups like 2:56, each group's notes in pitch order and no key twice in a row: J69 F67 D66 | F64 J66 K67 | F69 J70 F69 | J70 K72 J70 | D71 F73 J74 | K76 J74 F73 | J71 F70 J71 | F70 J72 F70; 3:10.1-3:18.2, m.217-226: the flute's quick burst 83 81 78 74 78 76 | 73 69 71 69 66 62 plays the same two K J F J F D waves as 3:03.7 (not D L D on the 69 71 69 turn: user, Nov 24: '3:11: what on earth is this DLD pattern?'); the first violins' 61 63 59 63 keeps 63 on J like the 62 before it; and their climb by a step up and a half step back (62 63 62 64 63 65 64 ... 74) rocks on two keys that move up with it, D F D F | J F J F | K J K J (each chunk ends on a step back so the next one steps up onto its new top key), instead of D J F F (the notes aren't doubled: '3:14 onwards: this DJFF pattern is weird. are the notes really duplicated?', then 'it's slowly going up right? can it be divided cleanly into chunks of DFDF FJFJ JKJK?'); 3:03.7-3:06.3, m.210-212: after the first violins' quick burst down (88 86 83 79 83 81 | 78 74 76 74 71 67 on two K J F J F D waves, which the user likes: 'aw, I liked the KJFJFD runs down'), the climb from 59 goes up in triplets F J K | F J K | F J K (one key up from the D67, not out to K and back: user, Nov 24: '3:05 -- there's a jump from D to K back to D. no good') and steps down to 73 on J (not F73 F67: '3:06 -- double F'); 3:02.0-3:03.5, m.208-209: the flute's falling groups of four, 88 86 83 79 | 83 81 78 74 | 76 74 71 67, play K J F D every time (user, Nov 24: 'at the very end here it goes into 4s, right?'); 2:56.0-3:01.9, m.201-207: the piccolo's and then the first violins' six-pitch figure goes by triplet groups, each group's notes in pitch order and no key twice in a row: J90 K92 | J94 F92 D90 | J89 F88 J89 | F88 D86 F88 | D89 F90 J92 | K94 J92 F90 | J89 F88 J89 | F88 D86 F88 | D83 F84 J86 | K88 J86 F84 | J83 F82 J83 | F82 D80 F82 | D83 F84 J86 | K88 J86 F84 (user, Nov 24: 'triplet groups makes the most sense to me, as long as nothing lands on the same note back to back'); 2:53.0-2:55.9, m.197-200: the first violins' 78 79 76 79 78 79 ... turns on F J K (76 78 79) instead of J78 J79 on one key, and 83 86 85 86 83 86 85 with the step down to 80 goes D K J K D K J F (the engine had F83 F86 and D85 K80); 2:32-2:39, the four falling eighth-note statements play on the tune's keys from 0:15-0:21, F D K F K J each time; 2:18.7-2:20.8, the figures that come back keep the keys they had the first time (bassoons 41 46 50 52 47 44 = D F J K F D, clarinets 53 58 62 64 59 56 = D F J K J F) and the flutes' 65 70 74 76 71 68 81 keep the D F J K F D K the user okayed; 2:15.65, the second held 64 on F like the first (same note, same key); 1:07.9-1:09.1, the six even notes rock D K D K D K and the tune comes in on K (user, Nov 21: 'I think it'd be six total notes? DKDKDK K(flute beginning)'). Notes: 1:19.7-2:12.3, the tune section laid out from the user's taps (three runs, Nov 21): every statement is one of the tune's two forms, 79 79 81 79 77 76 77 79 77 76 74 or ... 76 72 74 (an octave up on the celesta, an octave and two down for the horns and bassoons), in its written rhythm, starting where the user taps it (the two forms take turns all the way: at 1:37.5-1:47.8 A B A B, starting 97.47 / 99.97 / 102.62 / 105.13 by the user's taps, user: 'at 1:40 it plays the wrong form. It plays the second form a second time, which is wrong'); 2:00.8-2:12.3 B A B A (starting 120.79 / 123.45 / 126.04 / 128.76: the user's taps there, read one note on -- the chart had cut the 2:00.8 statement short; user: 'at 2:03, the same issue happens. The chart is wrong'), then 2:11.4-2:19.8 on the user's taps (three runs, Nov 22, medians): the flutes' 64 62 64 with the last 64 held from 2:12.28, the cellos' six-note figure 41 46 50 52 47 44 from 2:14.41, the 64 held again from 2:15.39 (key-pinned on F like the first), the clarinets' 53 58 62 64 59 56 from 2:17.25, the bassoons' 41 46 50 52 47 44 from 2:18.10, and the clarinets' 53 58 62 64 59 56 again from 2:19.07 (user: '2:19: clarinet triplets'), into the flutes at 2:19.9.",
